            <div xml:id="d1124">

                <pb facs="0811" n="695" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg695"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6363/32.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Secretary of the Navy</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 8, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith a
                    copy of a telegram dated May 1, from the special representative of the
                    Department of State at El Paso, Texas, quoting a telegram received by him, under
                    date of the 30th ultimo, from General Carranza, in relation to the resumption of
                    work in the Tampico oil district.</p>
                <p>I beg to request that the text of this telegram from General Carranza be
                    immediately telegraphed to Admiral Fletcher, for his information.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
